# Convert CLI into a FastAPI Server

This plan outlines the steps to convert the current pentest CLI into a robust FastAPI server. Since a pentest run is a long-running, multi-agent process, the server is designed to execute pentests asynchronously as background tasks. Users can start a pentest, monitor its status, cancel it, and stream real-time updates of the execution state.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Async Refactoring of LangGraph Nodes**
> To run the graph inside a FastAPI server (which already runs inside an active event loop), we must remove calls to `asyncio.run()` from within graph nodes (such as the executor and tactical planner) and convert these nodes into async functions (`async def`).
> 
> **Backwards Compatibility**
> The CLI entrypoint in [master_graph.py](file:///d:/Temp/langchain-academy/prototype/sub_agents/master_graph.py) will be modified to run the new async function via `asyncio.run()` at the top-level, keeping CLI capability intact.

> [!TIP]
> **Task Persistence Options**
> For the initial implementation, we propose an in-memory `TaskManager` that caches tasks and their states. For production, we can easily extend this to a SQLite database. We'll start with in-memory for speed and simplicity.

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> 1. **Streaming Choice**: Do you prefer **WebSockets** or **Server-Sent Events (SSE)** for streaming real-time status and state changes? SSE is recommended for read-only dashboards, while WebSockets are better for bi-directional communication.
> 2. **Port Number**: What port should the FastAPI server run on? We suggest `8000` by default.

