### FastAPI Web Server Integration

#### [NEW] [models.py](file:///d:/Temp/langchain-academy/app/api/models.py)
- Define Pydantic request models (e.g., `StartPentestRequest` containing `query` and `max_global_iterations`).
- Define Pydantic response models (e.g., `PentestTaskResponse` containing `task_id`, `status`, `current_phase`, `findings_count`, `final_answer`, etc.).

#### [NEW] [task_manager.py](file:///d:/Temp/langchain-academy/app/api/task_manager.py)
- Implement a thread-safe `TaskManager` class:
  - Cache tasks and their current `MasterState`.
  - Maintain a mapping of `task_id` to the active `asyncio.Task` object.
  - Expose helper methods to list all tasks, get a task's state, cancel a task (`task.cancel()`), and update task state during execution.
- Implement an async function to execute the LangGraph:
  - Runs the graph with `async for event in graph.astream(state):`.
  - On each step, updates the `TaskManager` cache with the latest state, current phase, objectives, and findings count.
  - Broadcasts updates to any subscribers (e.g. WebSocket queues).

#### [NEW] [routes.py](file:///d:/Temp/langchain-academy/app/api/routes.py)
- Define FastAPI routes:
  - `POST /api/pentest/start`: Trigger a new pentest task.
  - `GET /api/pentest/tasks`: List metadata of all tasks.
  - `GET /api/pentest/tasks/{task_id}`: Retrieve detailed state of a task.
  - `POST /api/pentest/tasks/{task_id}/cancel`: Cancel a running task.
  - `GET /api/pentest/tasks/{task_id}/stream`: WebSocket/SSE endpoint to stream real-time JSON events of the running task.

#### [NEW] [server.py](file:///d:/Temp/langchain-academy/app/server.py)
- Instantiate the FastAPI application.
- Setup CORS middleware to enable connection from a front-end interface.
- Include the routers from `routes.py`.
- Define CLI run command and main execution block.

